WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.293 --> 00:00:03.469
- He's a business man,
inventor, philanthropist

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.144
and television personality.

00:00:05.144 --> 00:00:09.169
- He has an estimated net
worth of 150 million dollars.

00:00:09.169 --> 00:00:13.156
- He leads close to 6,000
employees in over 100 cities

00:00:13.156 --> 00:00:14.609
across the U.S.

00:00:14.609 --> 00:00:17.295
- He is Marcus Lemonis and here are his

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:19.462
top ten rules for success.

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:26.461
- You know there's this myth
that people think they don't

00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:28.171
need a business plan.

00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:30.511
And often times I find business
owners who have an idea,

00:00:30.511 --> 00:00:31.864
a great one,

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:34.591
and where they miss it is the execution.

00:00:34.591 --> 00:00:37.346
They don't go through the
process of writing things down.

00:00:37.346 --> 00:00:39.252
Because any time you
can take pen to paper,

00:00:39.252 --> 00:00:42.756
write out your ideas and
share them with other people,

00:00:42.756 --> 00:00:44.178
and get feedback,

00:00:44.178 --> 00:00:46.458
which is essentially a business plan,

00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:47.881
you're going to do better.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.805
It could be a white
board in an office, uh,

00:00:50.805 --> 00:00:54.630
it could be notes taken on
your computer or in a journal.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.978
But I want it to start
with something that says

00:00:56.978 --> 00:00:59.510
here's what my product or service is,

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.192
here's how I'm going to attack the market,

00:01:02.192 --> 00:01:04.469
here's how I'm going to
beat the competition,

00:01:04.469 --> 00:01:06.696
here's how I'm going to
learn from my competitors,

00:01:06.696 --> 00:01:09.473
here's what I'm going to
take from my customers,

00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:10.998
and here's the kind of people I need

00:01:10.998 --> 00:01:12.575
to surround myself with.

00:01:12.575 --> 00:01:15.070
If you don't answer those
questions then really you're

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.836
just kind of, like a dodge ball game,

00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:19.852
you're just going to go
out there and wing it.

00:01:19.852 --> 00:01:21.832
And at some point you're going
to get whacked in the side

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:22.786
of the head.

00:01:22.786 --> 00:01:25.446
You know, cash flow to me is, is important

00:01:25.446 --> 00:01:29.295
but working capital from the
beginning is also important.

00:01:29.295 --> 00:01:31.741
I find people come to me
with a projection about their

00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:33.662
business, it's a brand new idea,

00:01:33.662 --> 00:01:36.056
they think they're going to
make money in six months,

00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:37.631
they don't make money in six months

00:01:37.631 --> 00:01:39.047
and they don't have a backup plan.

00:01:39.047 --> 00:01:41.511
They don't have a reserve, they
don't have a line of credit.

00:01:41.511 --> 00:01:44.143
And so they go out of
business and that's probably

00:01:44.143 --> 00:01:47.208
the single biggest reason
small businesses close,

00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:49.684
not because the idea is
terrible, not because they have

00:01:49.684 --> 00:01:52.344
bad people, they don't
have the sufficient amount

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.058
of working capital.

00:01:54.058 --> 00:01:56.617
One of the things that I do
do before I go to bed at night

00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.332
is I make a quick list of
the things that I know I have

00:01:59.332 --> 00:02:01.603
to deal with the next day.

00:02:01.603 --> 00:02:04.819
And I try to get those
knocked out before noon.

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:07.882
Because from noon on it's kind
of like the wild, wild west.

00:02:07.882 --> 00:02:09.611
I don't know what's going to happen.

00:02:09.611 --> 00:02:11.452
I don't know what new
issue is going to come up.

00:02:11.452 --> 00:02:14.224
And so you want to really be
smart about your time to knock

00:02:14.224 --> 00:02:15.742
out the things you have to.

00:02:15.742 --> 00:02:16.933
Who do I have to talk to?

00:02:16.933 --> 00:02:18.244
What do I have to review?

00:02:18.244 --> 00:02:20.422
What do I have to do with
a bank or an employee

00:02:20.422 --> 00:02:22.068
or one of the businesses?

00:02:22.068 --> 00:02:24.309
You want to get out, what
I call the housekeeping,

00:02:24.309 --> 00:02:26.224
you get the housekeeping
done in the morning

00:02:26.224 --> 00:02:28.904
and then you get to kind of
farm the fields for the rest

00:02:28.904 --> 00:02:29.737
of the day.

00:02:29.737 --> 00:02:31.871
And part of the challenge or
part of the challenge for me

00:02:31.871 --> 00:02:34.785
at least is that the lines get
very blurry of when the day

00:02:34.785 --> 00:02:36.628
actually shuts off.

00:02:36.628 --> 00:02:39.046
And that can present a real
challenge to, you know,

00:02:39.046 --> 00:02:41.208
your personal life and your friends

00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:43.725
and kind of that balance, so it's hard.

00:02:43.725 --> 00:02:46.264
But the first part of my day is the focus.

00:02:46.264 --> 00:02:48.940
I tell you, we need you here,

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.121
and this is more important
than any pie we'll ever make,

00:02:53.121 --> 00:02:55.765
but I'm going to need your
help before you leave,

00:02:55.765 --> 00:02:56.598
- [Woman] Absolutely.

00:02:56.598 --> 00:02:57.820
- Because I've got to get
some stuff done and you're

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.028
going to be our leader here.

00:02:59.028 --> 00:02:59.895
Okay?

00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:01.000
- Okay.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.390
- But in order for you to
be able to have good peace

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:07.141
of mind I wanted to give you some money.

00:03:07.141 --> 00:03:11.308
I'm going to give you six
month's worth of pay, okay?

00:03:14.623 --> 00:03:17.656
And when you come back you
will be fully in charge

00:03:17.656 --> 00:03:19.558
of this location.

00:03:19.558 --> 00:03:22.334
And I'm going to pay you $1000 a week,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:25.215
so you don't have to bartend, okay?

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:26.117
(crying)

00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:26.975
Okay.

00:03:26.975 --> 00:03:29.166
I'm going to give you a check.

00:03:29.166 --> 00:03:31.849
And it should help you just
kind of, be able to rest,

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:34.564
take care of your baby and
then when you come back

00:03:34.564 --> 00:03:35.963
you're going to bust somebody's ass.

00:03:35.963 --> 00:03:37.317
(laughs)

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.484
Alright, okay?

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.004
- Wow, thank you.

00:03:46.574 --> 00:03:49.661
- The reality of it is that
the employee is number one.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:53.280
Because if the employee is
happy, ultimately the customer

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.416
is going to be happy.

00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:56.934
If the employee is happy they're
going to take care of the

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.762
assets of your business.

00:03:58.762 --> 00:04:01.298
If the employee is happy
they will have a pride

00:04:01.298 --> 00:04:04.316
of ownership and they'll
stand side by side with you

00:04:04.316 --> 00:04:06.301
and they'll fight during the tough times

00:04:06.301 --> 00:04:08.533
and they'll celebrate
during the good times.

00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:11.352
If you take care of
your employees they will

00:04:11.352 --> 00:04:13.422
put the customer first.

00:04:13.422 --> 00:04:15.743
But if you don't, it won't matter.

00:04:15.743 --> 00:04:17.264
There won't be any customers.

00:04:17.264 --> 00:04:19.294
If you don't take care of
your employees there will be

00:04:19.294 --> 00:04:21.710
nobody to help and
you'll have no business.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.673
I say follow your passion,
which should be sports,

00:04:24.673 --> 00:04:27.433
I say if you have a passion
for business you also

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.312
better have a knowledge for it.

00:04:29.312 --> 00:04:31.735
And so if people want to own
a business they better have

00:04:31.735 --> 00:04:34.319
worked for somebody else for
a while and they better have

00:04:34.319 --> 00:04:36.763
an intrinsic knowledge of that industry.

00:04:36.763 --> 00:04:39.673
And so it would be like
me getting into, you know,

00:04:39.673 --> 00:04:41.431
the barber business and
I never went to learn

00:04:41.431 --> 00:04:42.769
how to cut hair.

00:04:42.769 --> 00:04:44.334
I should have a knowledge.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:47.806
If I don't have the knowledge
then I better have a partner

00:04:47.806 --> 00:04:51.313
or I better have a manager
or a leader in place who's

00:04:51.313 --> 00:04:54.415
vested in the business
who does have a knowledge.

00:04:54.415 --> 00:04:56.737
And so three guys want to
open up a restaurant because

00:04:56.737 --> 00:04:58.577
they think it's cool to open
up a restaurant but none

00:04:58.577 --> 00:05:01.070
of them know how to cook or wait tables,

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.583
they shouldn't be in that business.

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:07.264
Entrepreneurs who have
offered a product or a process

00:05:07.264 --> 00:05:10.845
that isn't working today
have to make the bold step

00:05:10.845 --> 00:05:13.012
of reinventing themselves.

00:05:14.335 --> 00:05:17.471
I talk about it all the time,
how over the course of my life

00:05:17.471 --> 00:05:19.572
whether it was at 12
years old or 18 years old,

00:05:19.572 --> 00:05:22.698
or 25 years old or even
today, I'm constantly working

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:24.428
to reinvent myself.

00:05:24.428 --> 00:05:27.392
I'm no different than
a package on a shelf,

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:29.299
people have to feel that it's relevant,

00:05:29.299 --> 00:05:30.956
they have to see the warning labels,

00:05:30.956 --> 00:05:32.218
they have to understand the contents,

00:05:32.218 --> 00:05:33.510
it has to be appealing,

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.980
it has to provide value to people.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.531
And so when an entrepreneur
has a product or a process that

00:05:38.531 --> 00:05:40.631
they've offered and they're
not willing to change it

00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:43.219
then they're going to
end up like Circuit City,

00:05:43.219 --> 00:05:45.636
or Montgomery Ward, or Sears,

00:05:47.053 --> 00:05:48.459
or Fiat or whatever these

00:05:48.459 --> 00:05:50.886
brands are that don't
exist anymore, right?

00:05:50.886 --> 00:05:54.197
Every single company
in this country today,

00:05:54.197 --> 00:05:57.394
if they're not evolving, they're dying.

00:05:57.394 --> 00:05:59.426
And I don't know why an
entrepreneur would think

00:05:59.426 --> 00:06:01.481
they're exempt from that process.

00:06:01.481 --> 00:06:03.613
I'm not interested in their
ego, I'm not interested in

00:06:03.613 --> 00:06:05.840
their pride, I'm not
interested in their feelings,

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.751
I'm interested in their
business being successful.

00:06:08.751 --> 00:06:11.839
And so I think not only does
their business have to do it

00:06:11.839 --> 00:06:15.672
but we as entrepreneurs
have to do it as well.

00:06:17.881 --> 00:06:19.494
Let's talk about the
myth that your product

00:06:19.494 --> 00:06:21.150
is already good enough.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.902
People often develop a new
product and it's fantastic

00:06:25.902 --> 00:06:28.810
and it hits the market,
like, in a blaze of glory,

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.816
and it sells and there's back orders.

00:06:30.816 --> 00:06:33.545
If you're delivering them a
good product or service today

00:06:33.545 --> 00:06:36.452
they're still going to expect
something better tomorrow.

00:06:36.452 --> 00:06:38.577
And the one thing you have
to worry about is there's

00:06:38.577 --> 00:06:40.285
a competitor out there,

00:06:40.285 --> 00:06:42.404
somebody that can mimic your offering.

00:06:42.404 --> 00:06:45.265
And so you always have to
stay one step ahead of them.

00:06:45.265 --> 00:06:49.145
And so when products don't
morph into something new,

00:06:49.145 --> 00:06:51.992
they don't develop into
something better and smarter

00:06:51.992 --> 00:06:55.146
and faster and less expensive,

00:06:55.146 --> 00:06:58.465
that's probably the biggest
takeaway, less expensive,

00:06:58.465 --> 00:07:01.198
then people are going
to find alternatives.

00:07:01.198 --> 00:07:03.850
For me I like to go out
and study the competition,

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.069
that's how I reinvent myself.

00:07:06.069 --> 00:07:09.502
I go out and I study businesses
that aren't exactly the same

00:07:09.502 --> 00:07:12.625
but they run their business
with a set of ethics

00:07:12.625 --> 00:07:15.199
and a set of principles
that are second to none,

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:17.486
and they can be in a space
that's completely different than

00:07:17.486 --> 00:07:21.098
mine but I learn something from them.

00:07:21.098 --> 00:07:23.209
I don't think we do that enough.

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:26.158
How many people you meet at
a party or at a restaurant

00:07:26.158 --> 00:07:28.290
that tell you they're entrepreneurs,

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.377
and in the past I used to say now,

00:07:30.377 --> 00:07:31.865
does that mean you don't work?

00:07:31.865 --> 00:07:32.698
- Mm.

00:07:32.698 --> 00:07:35.433
- And so an entrepreneur to me um,

00:07:35.433 --> 00:07:37.446
is kind of a nonsensical word.

00:07:37.446 --> 00:07:40.806
You're either a business owner
or you are a team member,

00:07:40.806 --> 00:07:41.711
one of the two.

00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:44.956
And I think being a business
owner is the hardest thing

00:07:44.956 --> 00:07:46.283
to do in this country.

00:07:46.283 --> 00:07:48.733
You take your money, hopefully
not your mother's money,

00:07:48.733 --> 00:07:51.577
but you take your money
and you invest in an idea

00:07:51.577 --> 00:07:53.914
which is essentially
investing in yourself,

00:07:53.914 --> 00:07:58.546
but if you do it solely to make
money you're going to lose.

00:07:58.546 --> 00:08:00.486
And you really have to do it
and I know that a lot of people

00:08:00.486 --> 00:08:02.880
out there get up every
morning and they hustle,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:03.713
- Right.

00:08:03.713 --> 00:08:04.812
- And they're driving in the
car right now and they're on

00:08:04.812 --> 00:08:06.738
their way to a job right
now that they may not love,

00:08:06.738 --> 00:08:07.571
- Yeah.

00:08:07.571 --> 00:08:10.106
- And, I encourage them
just to stick to the grind.

00:08:10.106 --> 00:08:12.555
Get the paycheck, pay the bills,

00:08:12.555 --> 00:08:14.124
learn, learn and learn.

00:08:14.124 --> 00:08:16.390
And too many young kids out
of college tell me they're

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.256
entrepreneurs and I tell them
you can't be an entrepreneur

00:08:18.256 --> 00:08:20.567
until you've worked for
somebody else and you know what

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.496
it feels like to be fired,

00:08:22.496 --> 00:08:23.329
- Right.

00:08:23.329 --> 00:08:24.860
- Or to be called on the
mat or to be harassed

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.148
or to be mismanaged,

00:08:26.148 --> 00:08:28.096
you've got to know what that
feels like so that when you're

00:08:28.096 --> 00:08:29.179
on the other side,

00:08:29.179 --> 00:08:30.012
- Yeah.

00:08:30.012 --> 00:08:30.970
- You can be respectful to people.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:31.803
- Yeah.

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:33.289
- You know I have a terrible fear

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:35.076
that I lay awake at night with,

00:08:35.076 --> 00:08:37.856
and that's the fear of failure
and the embarrassment that

00:08:37.856 --> 00:08:39.341
comes with it.

00:08:39.341 --> 00:08:42.060
And so people like to have a
lot of pride and say, you know,

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.313
I'm not embarrassed I'm not,

00:08:44.313 --> 00:08:47.863
I think anybody that's an
entrepreneur deep down,

00:08:47.863 --> 00:08:50.919
really deep down in their
soul has fear of failure.

00:08:50.919 --> 00:08:54.129
What will people say,
what will people think?

00:08:54.129 --> 00:08:56.526
And it's hard, it's a hard challenge.

00:08:56.526 --> 00:09:00.071
And so I try to ignore it as much as I can

00:09:00.071 --> 00:09:03.495
but I find it kind of haunting me.

00:09:03.495 --> 00:09:07.412
And so I push through because
I really believe that I have

00:09:07.412 --> 00:09:09.794
an obligation to keep trying
and trying and trying.

00:09:09.794 --> 00:09:12.176
And I've had plenty of failure in my life.

00:09:12.176 --> 00:09:15.341
What happened was when I turned 35,

00:09:15.341 --> 00:09:19.473
and 2008-9 happened, I
became much more comfortable

00:09:19.473 --> 00:09:21.760
with admitting my vulnerability,

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.700
acknowledging my mistakes,
saying when I was wrong,

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:28.756
showing my cards and
saying oh that was stupid.

00:09:28.756 --> 00:09:31.783
Crumbs could be one of those
situations where I tried

00:09:31.783 --> 00:09:33.851
to outsmart something and now,

00:09:33.851 --> 00:09:36.433
I don't think it's going to fail,

00:09:36.433 --> 00:09:38.905
but I have to be realistic, it could.

00:09:38.905 --> 00:09:40.356
Anything I do could fail.

00:09:40.356 --> 00:09:43.141
I go through thousands and
thousands of applications

00:09:43.141 --> 00:09:45.445
and sometimes I pick businesses
that are new and innovative

00:09:45.445 --> 00:09:47.729
and the product's exciting and
sometimes I pick businesses

00:09:47.729 --> 00:09:50.045
that are pretty ordinary.

00:09:50.045 --> 00:09:52.965
When it's ordinary and it's
saturated the biggest challenge

00:09:52.965 --> 00:09:54.689
is you're now dealing with a commodity,

00:09:54.689 --> 00:09:57.465
and so whether it's a
coffee shop or a yogurt shop

00:09:57.465 --> 00:10:01.392
the question is is the product
relevant in the marketplace?

00:10:01.392 --> 00:10:05.605
And if it's saturated can you
rise to the top of the list?

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:07.379
I want to encourage people not to

00:10:07.379 --> 00:10:10.237
run away from saturated markets,

00:10:10.237 --> 00:10:12.988
But I want you to run away
if you don't have the time,

00:10:12.988 --> 00:10:15.282
the resources, the energy, the people,

00:10:15.282 --> 00:10:20.245
the process or the attention
to detail to be best in class.

00:10:20.245 --> 00:10:21.669
And so if you're going to open up

00:10:21.669 --> 00:10:24.598
a coffee shop in a very crowded
market you'd better have

00:10:24.598 --> 00:10:26.104
something that's unique.

00:10:26.104 --> 00:10:27.904
It better be experiential.

00:10:27.904 --> 00:10:29.726
Your product better be amazing.

00:10:29.726 --> 00:10:32.826
You process better be on pointe.

00:10:32.826 --> 00:10:35.811
And the people that sell it
better be better in product

00:10:35.811 --> 00:10:38.231
knowledge and better in
experience than anything else.

00:10:38.231 --> 00:10:41.268
I guess a different way to
look at it is if you go into

00:10:41.268 --> 00:10:43.761
an industry that's not saturated

00:10:43.761 --> 00:10:46.049
you should probably ask
yourself is there a reason

00:10:46.049 --> 00:10:48.191
that nobody else is in this?

00:10:48.191 --> 00:10:51.179
I can't be the only person with this idea.

00:10:51.179 --> 00:10:53.990
And so you get into a
business that's not saturated

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:57.058
it may tell you that there's
not really a market there.

00:10:57.058 --> 00:11:00.098
I think I'd like to get
into the hanger business,

00:11:00.098 --> 00:11:02.463
I mean, is it saturated, is it not,

00:11:02.463 --> 00:11:05.060
is there a reason that
everybody's not in it.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.740
I don't really mind whether
it's saturated or not,

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:10.780
I have to like the product,
it has to be relatable.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:14.689
It has to be not totally recession proof,

00:11:14.689 --> 00:11:16.785
but it has to be kind of recession proof.

00:11:16.785 --> 00:11:18.140
I think it's important
that if you're going to get

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.192
into a business and you're
thinking about taking your

00:11:20.192 --> 00:11:22.017
last $50,000 and getting it,

00:11:22.017 --> 00:11:23.601
getting into something,

00:11:23.601 --> 00:11:25.777
you better have something
that is unique if it's going

00:11:25.777 --> 00:11:27.569
to be a commodity.

00:11:27.569 --> 00:11:31.125
And you better, better make
sure that you really understand

00:11:31.125 --> 00:11:33.210
what happens when the
economy goes up and down

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.721
and study those trends.

00:11:34.721 --> 00:11:37.039
- Thank you so much for watching,
I made this video because

00:11:37.039 --> 00:11:38.610
Black asked me to,

